@@ -8,24 +8,33 @@ npm start        # http://localhost:3000, data in tasks.db (PORT and DB_PATH cha
 npm test         # the API tests (node:test)
 ```
 
 ## API
 
-Every body is JSON. A task is `{ "id": 1, "title": "Buy milk", "done": false, "created_at": "2026-01-31T09:00:00.000Z" }`.
+Every body is JSON. A task is `{ "id": 1, "title": "Buy milk", "done": false, "created_at": "2026-01-31T09:00:00.000Z", "tags": ["home", "shop"] }`.
 
 | Method and path | What it does | Answers |
 |---|---|---|
-| `GET /api/tasks` | Lists the tasks, oldest first; `?done=true` or `?done=false` keeps the done or the open ones | 200, an array of tasks |
-| `POST /api/tasks` | Creates a task from `{ "title": "…" }` | 201, the task |
+| `GET /api/tasks` | Lists the tasks, oldest first; `?done=true` or `?done=false` keeps the done or the open ones; `?tag=home` keeps the tasks with that tag (the two combine) | 200, an array of tasks, or 400 `{ "error": "invalid tags" }` for an invalid `tag` |
+| `POST /api/tasks` | Creates a task from `{ "title": "…", "tags": ["home"] }` (`tags` is optional) | 201, the task, or 400 `{ "error": "invalid tags" }` |
 | `GET /api/tasks/:id` | Reads a task | 200, or 404 `{ "error": "task not found" }` |
-| `PATCH /api/tasks/:id` | Changes `title` and / or `done` | 200, the task, or 404 |
-| `DELETE /api/tasks/:id` | Deletes a task | 204, or 404 |
+| `PATCH /api/tasks/:id` | Changes `title`, `done` and / or `tags` | 200, the task, 404, or 400 `{ "error": "invalid tags" }` |
+| `DELETE /api/tasks/:id` | Deletes a task and its links to tags | 204, or 404 |
+| `GET /api/tags` | Lists the tags in use with their number of tasks, sorted by name | 200, `[{ "name": "home", "count": 2 }, { "name": "work", "count": 1 }]` |
 
 Errors answer `{ "error": "<message>" }`.
 
+### Tags
+
+- Every task has `tags`: an array of strings sorted alphabetically, `[]` by default.
+- Each tag is trimmed and lowercased, and duplicates are removed. A valid tag is then 1 to 30 characters among `a-z`, `0-9` and `-`, and a task has at most 10 tags. The `tag` of `GET /api/tasks` is normalized and checked the same way.
+- In a PATCH, `tags` replaces the whole list (`[]` clears it); a PATCH without `tags` leaves them as they are.
+- A `tags` that is not an array of valid strings answers 400 `{ "error": "invalid tags" }` and nothing changes.
+- `GET /api/tags` does not list a tag that no task uses any more.
+
 ## Layout
 
-- `src/db.ts`: opens the database and runs the migrations (`PRAGMA user_version` counts those applied).
+- `src/db.ts`: opens the database and runs the migrations (`PRAGMA user_version` counts those applied). Tags live in their own tables: `tags` (one row per name) and `task_tags` (the links between tasks and tags, removed with their task).
 - `src/tasks.ts`: the queries.
 - `src/app.ts`: the HTTP server and its routes.
 - `public/`: the page.
 - `test/`: the API tests, against a server on a random port with an in-memory database.
